from pathlib import Path
import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
clips=json.loads((ROOT/'source_assets/animations/manifest.json').read_text());contracts=json.loads((ROOT/'source_assets/animations/contact_contracts.json').read_text())
text=['# Animation manifest — v0.4','','**Real animated exports, contact-constrained procedural studies. Animator and GTA acceptance remain outstanding.**','','Editable source: `source_assets/animations/GenesisAnimations.blend`; hierarchy: `rig.json`; contact windows and anatomical proxies: `contact_contracts.json`; export settings/pole calibration: `export_settings.json`. Motion authoring: `tools/animation_profiles.py` + `tools/build_animations.py`.','','| Clip | Frames inclusive | Seconds | FPS | Loop |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for c in clips:text.append(f"| {c['name']} | 1–{c['frames'][1]} | {c['seconds']} | 30 | {'yes' if c['loop'] else 'no'} |")
text+=['','## Contact contract','Each clip declares planted intervals for each foot. Root and wrist/ankle targets are evaluated every frame on the source and after FBX reimport. Sole proxies are offset from the foot bone onto a reference Z=0 plane; these are **not** mesh collision samples. Held-grip intervals measure both palm-centre proxies against a +Y line at X=0, Z=1.05; this is not finger contact. Non-applicable foot/grip metrics are recorded as null.','', 'Tolerance: 0.002 m (2 mm) for proxy contact and target reach. Root translation test tolerance: 0.0001 m. Detailed actual values, applicable sample counts, hashes and failures are in `tests/animation_contact_results.json`. A failed contract aborts the full build. Ten explicitly supported end→start transition pairs are compared on all deform-bone matrices in both source and imported FBX; unsupported pairs still require blending.','', '## Walking and jump phases','`GB_CautiousWalk` remains in-place. Translate the actor by +0.88 m in source +Y per 3-second cycle (approximately 0.2933 m/s) to keep its stance proxies stationary relative to the floor. Validation applies this explicit virtual actor drive; it does not claim a stationary actor has planted feet in an in-place walk. Swing uses Hermite velocity matching.','`GB_Jump` has planted preparation through normalized time 0.2, flight to 0.8, then planted landing/recovery. Probe/stumble/short-step clips lift the moving foot; intentional slip/fall phases are not misclassified as planted stance.','', '## Export / import timing','Binary FBX 7400, 30 FPS, metres, source Z-up/+Y facing → FBX -Z forward/Y up. Deform-only, armature-only, no leaf bones, every-frame bake, no simplification. Individual exports contain one action; combined `Genesis_All.fbx` contains 20.','Blender importer defaults to a +1-frame animation offset. Validation explicitly sets `anim_offset=0` and checks exact 1..N frame spans. The default importer offset is not a corrupt FBX timeline. No implicit resampling or one-frame timing shift is accepted in contact checks.','', '## Leaf-bone marker caveat','With no leaf bones, FBX importers may invent terminal bone **display lengths**. Do not use an imported display tail as an anatomical toe/palm landmark. Validation uses the source anatomical marker vectors stored in `contact_contracts.json` transformed by the actual imported bone matrix.','', '## Rig and conversion','Custom 26-bone rig: 18 deform bones, 4 IK endpoint controls and 4 pole controls. Deform-only FBX excludes all eight controls. Foot/hand world orientation constraints are baked to deform tracks. No fingers, toes, clavicles, final skin, verified GTA bone IDs or IFP files are supplied. See `retargeting.md`.','', '## Inspection','Optional actual source-rig GIFs: `python tools/render_animation_previews.py`. The cautious-walk inspection applies the documented actor drive. `tests/animation_preview_results.json` records source/image hashes if rendered. These diagnostics are not MTA playback, a final character or animator sign-off.']
(ROOT/'docs/animation_manifest.md').write_text('\n'.join(text)+'\n')
